WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:07.180
To Kenya now, where a series of grim discoveries
in a river have local residents scared and

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:09.200
authorities looking for answers.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.790
For months, dead bodies have been dumped into
the River Yala.

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:17.660
It's unclear who the people are, how they
died, or who is deposing of them.

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:21.150
DW's Felix Maringa has more on the mystery.

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:28.750
The river Yala pours into Africa’s largest
lake, Lake Victoria.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:33.210
For months now, local residents have been
making a gruesome find – dead bodies in

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:39.890
various states of decomposition, that have
been dumped in the river.

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:42.649
I have no idea where these bodies are coming
from.

00:00:42.649 --> 00:00:48.050
They are bound - some have their head tied
with nylon, other bodies are in a sack, others

00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:51.640
have their hands tied.

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:56.309
People say some of the bodies they have found
show signs of mutilation or torture.

00:00:56.309 --> 00:01:00.339
But the local doctor says he has found nothing
suspicious.

00:01:00.339 --> 00:01:07.150
the type of injury that is manifested is basically
drowning.

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:10.830
We are not able to ascertain whether there
is any other type of injury on these bodies,

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:15.570
unless and until a postmortem is conducted.

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:19.540
Police and activist groups are giving differing
accounts of the number of dead.

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:25.140
Rights group Amnesty International has voiced
its concern and accuses authorities of down-playing

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:26.320
the matter.

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:32.600
We are here because we know that a minimum
of thirty bodies, a minimum of thirty bodies

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:35.610
have been found in the last 6 months.

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:41.110
So do not let anybody teach us or cheat us
that there were thirty bodies over the last

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:45.840
two years, that is not the truth, it is not
the truth.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:49.360
Even more bodies have been retrieved from
the river this week.

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:53.920
People hoping to find missing relatives among
the dead have travelled from as far away as

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:56.570
Mombasa on the coast.

00:01:56.570 --> 00:02:01.620
No one knows where these bodies are coming
from because this river is quite lengthy it’s

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:08.700
about 200 kilometers long, so the bodies could
be coming from even the neighboring counties.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:15.120
Local police have been unable to provide answers,
leaving residents in the area terrified.

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:20.700
I’m afraid because I often watch football
at the local bars at night.

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:24.989
But now that we’re finding these bodies,
I’m afraid of meeting these people who are

00:02:24.989 --> 00:02:26.379
dumping bodies in the river.

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:29.489
If they see you, they might kill you and dump
you too.

00:02:29.489 --> 00:02:37.939
So that makes me afraid of being out at night
An investigative team from the capital Nairobi

00:02:37.939 --> 00:02:46.090
has arrived to find out why these bodies are
being dumped in the river and who is responsible.

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:50.739
Until then, the river Yala will continue to
hold the secret to this grim mystery.

